WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.989 --> 00:00:08.220
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and you are cordially
invited to the wedding of Joffrey Baratheon

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.620
and Margaery Tyrell.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:12.700
So what I wanted to do for this week’s bonus
video was dive deep into the Purple Wedding

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.030
itself, what’s going on around it, catch
up with all the running plot threads and some

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:20.450
important things that are going on off to
the side of this epic party they’re throwing.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:24.890
My video tonight will be my regular episode
review, if you’re finding me for the first

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:27.259
time be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:31.359
Every week I do episode videos as well as
a couple bonus videos and a weekly giveaway.

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:33.140
So just to avoid mega spoilers for people
who haven’t read the books, please be nice

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.800
in the comments until after the episode airs.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.620
Let’s get going.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.410
There’s so much to talk about including
the production itself, the actual wedding

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:45.490
and banquet and all the side stories happening
around it.

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:49.840
I’m going to start with some context, WTF
is it called the purple wedding if it was

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.400
never called that in the books.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:58.140
The answer is because of the show and the
Red Wedding last year.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.870
The color purple was chosen because of the
color of the macguffin.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:06.350
Which I will not utter here.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:12.850
Essentially there’s this small thing that
goes overlooked and ends up being really important.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:16.030
And it just happens to be purple.

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:20.869
The term is never used in the books, but because
the Red Wedding episode last year became so

00:01:20.869 --> 00:01:22.601
popular, colored weddings became a thing.

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:23.601
Almost like any new marriage in a song of
ice and fire is doomed.

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:24.601
So if you ever found yourself in Westeros,
just avoid marriage all together.

00:01:24.601 --> 00:01:25.601
It hasn’t worked out for any of the main
characters so far.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:26.601
Just ask Sansa how happy she is being married
to Tyrion.

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:27.601
Now we know why it’s called the purple wedding,
but there’s so much more going on besides

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:28.601
the wedding and the banquet.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:31.710
It’s easy to get distracted with all the
shinyness in the trailers.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.649
As epic is the wedding is, remember it almost
didn’t happen.

00:01:34.649 --> 00:01:45.689
One of the biggest threats against the crown
in the last few seasons has been bankruptcy.

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:50.520
Remember Littlefinger revealed to Catelyn
that he had gone to Great Gatsby lengths to

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.520
destabilize the crown using debt so that chaos
would erupt and he might be able to be with

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:56.520
her.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:57.719
Freaking crazy, I know right.

00:01:57.719 --> 00:02:01.810
If you didn’t think he was nuts before all
the Sansa creeping and brothel scenes, the

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:05.060
Chaos Is A Ladder speech really sealed the
door on him.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.939
Even Varys was a little disgusted by him.

00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:09.890
And he was keeping someone locked in a box.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.340
So for all intents and purposes.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:15.040
The Crown or the Monarchy is broke.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.750
The Baratheons might still have some money,
but Stannis pretty much burnt it all when

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:22.310
all those ships blew up in the Battle of Blackwater.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.970
And even he was borrowing them on credit.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:28.170
We haven’t seen him yet, but Mark Gatiss
is playing a character from the Iron Bank

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.170
of Braavos.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.070
I can only imagine what they’ll do if they
don’t get their money.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:35.370
Ever since Tywin has been in power though,
the crown has borrowed money from the Lannisters.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:39.420
At a pretty stiff interest rate and the rich
get richer.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.980
Once Joffrey took the throne he forgave all
that debt.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.930
But they still owe millions of gold coins
to the Iron Bank.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:50.590
So not only is the Iron Bank going to come
for Stannis eventually, it will come for King’s

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:51.590
Landing.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:56.340
Or it’s possible that they could turn around
and fund their enemies, which really is just

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.340
Danaerys.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.760
That’s really one big way to win a war.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.810
Cut off your enemies supply of money and fund
their enemies.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:05.700
This is why we saw that scene between Tywin
and The Queen of Thorns last season where

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.970
they haggled over who would pay for Joffrey
and Margaerys wedding.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:11.080
Because the crown itself could not.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:13.560
Think about the war of the five kings this
way now.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.050
Anyone who becomes king next, will inherit
all that debt.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.600
So ask yourself, how bad do you really want
the Iron Throne.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:26.310
Now that we understand the shitstorm of debt
and the Iron Bank brewing around King’s

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:30.530
Landing, let’s talk about them shooting
the actual episode itself.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:34.160
The way the actors talked about it made it
seem like it was designed to be the most epic

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:35.850
wedding in the history of Westeros.

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:39.950
I can’t imagine all the Targaryen’s went
too crazy with their weddings since they were

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.930
sisterwiving so much.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:46.020
So that’s why in all the clips we’ve seen,
the wedding itself looks really garish.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:50.010
Like putting gold rims on an old car when
you don’t have any money.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:55.590
Charles Dance actually said that the wedding
and the banquet felt like a short film because

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:56.960
the production was so elaborate.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:02.990
They ended up having more extras and people
on set those days than any episode since the

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:04.370
premiere.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:08.570
I think the season 1 premiere is still technically
the largest episode in terms of characters

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:09.670
on screen.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:11.810
But if you look at these behind the scenes
pictures.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:16.370
You can almost see every single character
associated with King’s Landing, every character

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:19.310
that has appeared on screen in King’s Landing.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:20.599
That’s a lot of people.

00:04:20.599 --> 00:04:25.840
So one of the things I’m most looking forward
to is just how crazy everything looks with

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.220
all the people, the huge sets and props.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.560
Game Of Thrones has some of the best sets
and costumes.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.650
Just look at the amount of detail that went
into Jaime’s golden hand.

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:40.919
I loved when they just casually dismissed
it, as if Cersei just found it in a dime store

00:04:40.919 --> 00:04:42.370
in Fleabottom.

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:43.630
But now let’s talk about Sansa.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:48.639
Surprisingly, in all this, she has a real
reason to be happy.

00:04:48.639 --> 00:04:53.500
It’s implied, or she thinks it’s implied
that once Joffrey marries Margaery, his attention

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.820
span for torturing her will just fade away.

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:59.520
And he’ll just start devoting himself to
being horrible to Margaery.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:03.289
During her wedding to Tyrion last year he
did kind of say he’d never be completely

00:05:03.289 --> 00:05:04.889
“done” tormenting her.

00:05:04.889 --> 00:05:09.009
But if it’s so easy for Tyrion to make him
froth at the mouth, I think Margaery would

00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:12.050
be able to handle him.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:21.849
Last week in the premiere we also got to see
a really nice scene with The Queen 

00:05:21.849 --> 00:05:22.849
of Thorns.

00:05:22.849 --> 00:05:28.520
She’s so formidable, I think of her as a
female Tywin.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:30.500
They are pretty evenly matched.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.380
And she has been learning all about Joffrey’s
true nature.

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:38.110
So just because Margaery is willing to jump
into bed with the monster, doesn’t mean

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:40.360
her family isn’t taking steps to protect
her.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:44.080
That being said, I think the people I’ll
be watching most closely during the episode

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:46.350
are Joffrey and Margaery of course.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:49.719
Sansa and Tyrion and The Queen of Thorns.

00:05:49.719 --> 00:05:51.400
There’s so many more crazy things that will
happen in the episode and at the wedding it’s

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.270
really hard to just pick a few characters
to follow.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:56.270
Bran is going to have few new scenes on his
journey to find the three eyed raven beyond

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:57.270
the wall.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:02.889
I’m really interested to see how those scenes
work against the wedding scenes.

00:06:02.889 --> 00:06:09.749
All 
that being said, let me know what you’re

00:06:09.749 --> 00:06:11.120
looking forward to most.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:14.590
The wedding itself, Bran’s scenes.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:17.080
Or do you think there will be some surprise
Stannis moments.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:24.400
Like I said, I’ll dive way deeper into specific
moments in my episode review and explain a

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.800
lot more about the purple macguffin.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:27.560
And remember, round 2 of the giveaway starts
as soon as I post that video.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:31.039
All you have to do is be a subscriber and
leave a comment.

00:06:31.039 --> 00:06:32.669
You can click here for that video.

00:06:32.669 --> 00:06:34.990
I’ll add the annotation when I post it tonight.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.059
And click here for last week’s episode.

00:06:37.059 --> 00:06:40.210
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

